Since this project targets net9.0, the `#if NET6_0_OR_GREATER` condition is always true. Replace each block that follows this pattern:

```csharp
#if NET6_0_OR_GREATER
				writer.WriteRawValue(SOMETHING);
#else
                using (JsonDocument document = JsonDocument.Parse(SOMETHING, ModelSerializationExtensions.JsonDocumentOptions))
                {
                    JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, document.RootElement);
                }
#endif
```

with just:
```csharp
                writer.WriteRawValue(SOMETHING);
```

Note: the indentation of the `#if` block uses tabs (the `writer.WriteRawValue` line), while the `#else` block uses spaces. Use the same indentation as the surrounding code (spaces, matching the indentation of the `#if` line).

Find ALL files in the project that have this pattern and fix them all. Use `grep -rn` to find all occurrences, then edit each one.

IMPORTANT: Preserve the exact variable name used in each occurrence (it could be `item.Value`, `Template`, `Properties`, `PolicyRule`, etc. - whatever the argument to both WriteRawValue and JsonDocument.Parse is).

